.\" hydra-bench(1)
.TH HYDRA\-BENCH 1 "2026-08-17" "hydra" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
hydra-bench \- measurement harnesses for scheduler and transport
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hydra bench
.RI [ \-\-real ]
.RI [ \-\-reps " N" ]
.RI [ \-\-which " HARNESS" ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the measurement harnesses the project's results were produced with.
This is a development and validation tool, not part of the download path.
.PP
Without
.BR \-\-real ,
harnesses run against an in-process origin over a duplex pipe: hermetic,
repeatable, and unaffected by whatever the network is doing.
With
.BR \-\-real ,
objects are fetched over the network from public mirrors, which is the only
way to check that a simulator result survives contact with a real server.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-real
Download real objects over the network instead of running a simulated
harness.
Ignores
.BR \-\-which .
.TP
.BI \-\-reps " N"
Repetitions.
Default 3.
.TP
.BI \-\-which " HARNESS"
Which harness to run.
Default
.BR xval .
.RS
.TP
.B xval
Cross-validation: simulator against real HTTP, on matched parameters.
.TP
.B memprofile
Resident memory against object size.
The transport uses positioned writes and holds no reassembly buffer, so this
is the measurement that shows memory not tracking file size.
.TP
.B ticksweep
Makespan against the scheduler tick.
.TP
.B sizesweep
Detection-lag amortisation against object size.
.TP
.B detectab
A/B comparison of the collapse detector.
.RE
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The harness ran.
.TP
.B 2
Unknown harness name.
.PP
Note that the exit status reports whether the harness
.I ran,
not whether the numbers it produced were good.
Read the output.
.
.SH NOTES
.B \-\-real
requires outbound network access and, in a proxied environment, a proxy in
.B http_proxy
or
.BR HTTP_PROXY :
the real-network harness targets mirrors through it and fails without one.
.PP
A measurement taken over an in-process pipe does not measure latency.
Where a protocol cost is inherently about round trips \(em FTP preemption,
for instance \(em the project reports round-trip
.I counts
rather than durations, because a count is a protocol property that carries
to a real network while a duration measured over a pipe does not.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
hydra bench                          # xval, 3 reps
hydra bench \-\-which memprofile
hydra bench \-\-real \-\-reps 5
.fi
.RE
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hydra (1)
.PP
.IR docs/results/ ", " crossvalidation.md .
